  "body": "Positioned in the thriving heart of Stanmore Bay, this exceptional development site at 619 Whangaparaoa Road (also known as 17A Arklow Road) offers a rare opportunity to commence construction immediately, without the uncertainty, delays, and costs typically associated with the consent process.\r\n\r\nSet on an 867m² Business – Mixed Use zoned site, this premium project comes with Resource Consent (RC), Building Consent (BC), and Engineering Plan Approval (EPA) already secured, allowing developers and investors to move straight from acquisition to construction.\r\n\r\nDevelopment Highlights\r\n8 architecturally designed terrace homes\r\nModern multi-level layout designed to maximize elevation, outlook, and natural light\r\nPrivate outdoor living spaces and functional floorplans\r\nDedicated resident parking court\r\nEPA-approved infrastructure and service connections ready for implementation\r\nOptimized design that makes full use of the site’s natural topography\r\nOutstanding Location\r\nFuture residents will enjoy the convenience of one of the Hibiscus Coast’s most sought-after locations:\r\n\r\nWalking distance to Coast Plaza, supermarkets, cafés, and everyday amenities\r\nMinutes from Stanmore Bay Beach and Stanmore Bay Leisure Centre\r\nExcellent accessibility with dual frontage and address profile\r\nClose to schools, public transport, and recreational facilities\r\nA Smarter Development Investment\r\nIn today’s environment, securing a project with approvals already in place provides a significant competitive advantage. Avoid lengthy consent timelines, reduce holding costs, and minimise regulatory risk while bringing a proven development concept to market faster.\r\n\r\nWhether you’re an experienced developer looking for your next project or an investor seeking a de-risked opportunity with substantial upside, this is a turnkey development package ready for action.\r\n\r\nThe planning is complete. The approvals are secured. The opportunity is ready.\r\n\r\nContact us today for further information and to secure this outstanding Stanmore Bay development opportunity.",
